{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Despite its significance, OH remains largely unintegrated into national governance and service delivery structures, with limited coordination across human health, animal health and environmental sectors [ 14 ], and only a few countries demonstrating uneven progress toward cross-sectoral integration [ 16 ].\n...\nAs a result, there remains limited clarity on how governance arrangements, financing mechanisms, workforce capacity and institutional coordination collectively influence the integration of OH into national health systems.",
      "reason": "Describes gaps/uncertainties in existing knowledge (limited clarity on how key health-system functions collectively influence OH integration)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Despite its significance, OH remains largely unintegrated into national governance and service delivery structures, with limited coordination across human health, animal health and environmental sectors [ 14 ], and only a few countries demonstrating uneven progress toward cross-sectoral integration [ 16 ].\n...\nAccordingly, this systematic review synthesizes global evidence on the challenges and opportunities of integrating OH into national health systems across human, animal and environmental sectors and identifies actionable system-level strategies to support sustainable integration.",
      "reason": "Explains why the review is needed by highlighting the lack of integration/coordination and stating that the review will synthesize evidence and identify strategies."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "More recent reviews published in 2025 [ 30-32 ] have examined operational challenges in rural African contexts, ethical considerations within a globalized OH framework and critical reflections from the Global South. Although these contributions broaden thematic and regional understanding, they primarily focus on conceptual or context-specific dimensions rather than systematically analysing how implementation barriers and facilitators intersect with core health system functions.\n\nAs a result, there remains limited clarity on how governance arrangements, financing mechanisms, workforce capacity and institutional coordination collectively influence the integration of OH into national health systems.\n\nA comparative synthesis is therefore necessary to identify recurring structural barriers and enabling factors across diverse contexts.",
      "reason": "Cites other (recent) reviews and explains why a new review is required based on limitations of those prior reviews."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not describe an intervention effects review or a proposed mechanism of action for an intervention; the review is described as synthesizing implementation challenges/opportunities for integrating One Health."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not present a logic model to hypothesise relationships between intervention components and outcomes; the focus is on integration challenges/opportunities and system-level strategies rather than a logic-modelled intervention."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 74
}

{
